2026-11-08-record-foundation.md
docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:1:# Concrete Lean foundation proposal — draft 3
docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:5:The [A2i decision](../decisions.md#decided-project-long-term-2026-11-06) freezes integrated scopes, "not an untested whole-language architecture". Here the frozen foundation means interfaces and laws implemented, proved and tested together, with representative interactions. It does not mean designing every future slice before slice 1. Later slices supply lawful instances; changes to decided rules return to the owner.
docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:13:The foundation comprises target profiles; typed identities; types, values and places; control and calls; scalar operations; layout and representation; byte memory; ownership, loans, brands and authority; observations and leakage; evaluator adequacy; primitive contracts; frames and ABI; evidence, facts and diagnostics. An interface includes its state, preconditions, results and preservation laws, not just a record of names.
docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:127:**Authority:** Core Q1.5, Q6.3, Q9.1–Q9.2, Q9.6–Q9.7, Q9.10–Q9.13; [OD81](../decisions.md#od81), [OD125](../decisions.md#od125), [pipeline](../decisions.md#decided-project-pipeline-2026-11-06), [early evidence](../decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-early-evidence). **Later:** primitive instances and syntax, module/invariant checking at 17. Q9.7's exhaustive inventory becomes exhaustive coverage of the selected registry, not a permanently closed universe.
docs/proposals/FOUNDATION.md:181:<a id="q5"></a>**Q5. Niches.** Three options: (a) exactly one null-empty/non-null single-pointer-payload niche, with pointer-size, provenance, ownership and release-context proofs; (b) tagged layout now, future niches only by owner decision; (c) no niches permanently. Recommend **(b)**: the foundation needs representation laws, not a permanent optimization inventory. Runner-up **(a)** gives compact optional ownership but adds a special eligibility proof; multiword release contexts and nullable raw pointers are ineligible. Round-2 reviewers split: Codex and Kimi prefer (b); agy prefers (c). (c) is uniform but unnecessarily permanent.
